 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you today? It' simple but big choice. Want faster computers that last years, or cheaper ones that need replacing every few months? Sure thing. The one you supposed lead has been rescheduled without telling you. To a time that conflicts with another meeting. If they do, they' keeping it themselves. If not, it's a surprise. You got it. That it comes down to whether you want fast computer that lasts, or one that's cheap to buy but needs replacing soon. Then think about how long you want this computer to last. Then double it. That's how long the fast one will last too. A cheap one needs replacing every few months, so count the savings over each month.",
